1
00:00:09,444 --> 00:00:12,969
The chain ends when ignorance
ends. But what was ignorance?

2
00:00:13,049 --> 00:00:14,790
Not a thing to be destroyed.

3
00:00:14,870 --> 00:00:16,696
A way of taking things.

4
00:00:17,512 --> 00:00:20,140
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

5
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:24,098
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

6
00:00:24,908 --> 00:00:28,949
Part 1 set out how Nāgārjuna
reads when this is, that is.

7
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:31,857
A pattern holding, with
nothing handed over.

8
00:00:31,937 --> 00:00:35,023
Part 2 followed the twelve links
through his chapter on them.

9
00:00:35,103 --> 00:00:38,628
Karma and rebirth kept, and
only the owner left out.

10
00:00:39,432 --> 00:00:44,207
Section 5 took up, in the tradition's
own terms, where the chain is cut.

11
00:00:44,287 --> 00:00:47,495
Here I take up the same
ending, as Nāgārjuna reads it.

12
00:00:47,575 --> 00:00:50,122
This part closes Section 6.

13
00:00:50,932 --> 00:00:54,389
When ignorance has ceased,
formations do not arise.

14
00:00:54,469 --> 00:00:57,813
And ignorance ceases through
cultivating this very knowledge.

15
00:00:57,893 --> 00:01:01,418
By the ceasing of each link,
the next does not arise.

16
00:01:02,216 --> 00:01:05,360
So far, this is the
tradition's own teaching.

17
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,444
The difference is in what is ending.

18
00:01:08,244 --> 00:01:11,275
If the links were real events,
each with its own nature,

19
00:01:11,355 --> 00:01:14,713
the reverse order would mean
stopping a chain of real things,

20
00:01:14,793 --> 00:01:17,883
as one stops a machine.
And it could not be done.

21
00:01:17,963 --> 00:01:20,931
A link with its own nature
could not be removed.

22
00:01:21,736 --> 00:01:25,098
For Nāgārjuna, nothing
real has to be destroyed.

23
00:01:25,178 --> 00:01:28,698
When this is not, that is
not, is the same pattern,

24
00:01:28,778 --> 00:01:30,424
seen from its other side.

25
00:01:30,504 --> 00:01:33,563
The links were never handed
over from one to the next.

26
00:01:33,643 --> 00:01:36,878
They held together as a pattern
while ignorance was present.

27
00:01:36,958 --> 00:01:40,401
When ignorance is absent,
the pattern does not hold.

28
00:01:41,204 --> 00:01:45,816
Nothing is broken, because nothing was
ever standing on its own to be broken.

29
00:01:46,632 --> 00:01:48,771
What is the knowledge that ends ignorance?

30
00:01:48,851 --> 00:01:53,092
Candrakīrti reads it as seeing
dependent arising as it really is.

31
00:01:53,172 --> 00:01:55,093
Which is seeing its emptiness.

32
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:58,714
The tradition sees things
arising and passing,

33
00:01:58,794 --> 00:02:00,539
and lets go of a self among them.

34
00:02:00,619 --> 00:02:03,202
Nāgārjuna does not set that aside.

35
00:02:03,282 --> 00:02:05,145
He takes it one step further.

36
00:02:05,225 --> 00:02:08,487
He asks about the arising
and passing itself.

37
00:02:08,567 --> 00:02:11,304
Is arising found, when it is looked for?

38
00:02:12,104 --> 00:02:15,067
So the seeing that ends
ignorance is not only,

39
00:02:15,147 --> 00:02:18,197
this arises and passes, and is not mine.

40
00:02:18,277 --> 00:02:22,490
It is, this was never found to
arise, and never found to pass,

41
00:02:22,570 --> 00:02:23,931
as a thing on its own.

42
00:02:24,011 --> 00:02:29,044
That is why he praises dependent arising
as without arising, and without ceasing.

43
00:02:29,844 --> 00:02:33,722
Nāgārjuna also gives the order
in which the chain takes hold.

44
00:02:33,802 --> 00:02:37,241
Action and affliction come
from conceptual construction.

45
00:02:37,321 --> 00:02:39,171
And these come from elaboration.

46
00:02:39,251 --> 00:02:41,648
Elaboration stops in emptiness.

47
00:02:42,448 --> 00:02:48,011
Elaboration is the mind's spinning.
It is. It is not. It arises.

48
00:02:48,091 --> 00:02:51,190
It ceases. Mine. Not mine.

49
00:02:51,270 --> 00:02:54,913
It is the same habit as asking
of anything what it really is,

50
00:02:54,993 --> 00:02:56,915
and needing a something to be there.

51
00:02:57,716 --> 00:03:03,716
Notice where elaboration stops. Not in
silence. Not in a blank. In emptiness.

52
00:03:04,052 --> 00:03:07,808
In seeing that what elaboration
keeps fixing was never fixed.

53
00:03:08,616 --> 00:03:11,729
A quiet mind can rest from
elaborating for a while,

54
00:03:11,809 --> 00:03:14,818
and then begin again, because
nothing has been seen.

55
00:03:14,898 --> 00:03:18,799
When emptiness is seen, elaboration
has nothing to stand on.

56
00:03:18,879 --> 00:03:20,524
Not because thought is stopped.

57
00:03:20,604 --> 00:03:23,776
Because what thought was building
on is found not to be there.

58
00:03:24,580 --> 00:03:27,072
Here I part from one way
of hearing the teaching.

59
00:03:27,152 --> 00:03:30,238
Some say that dependent
arising begins with ignorance,

60
00:03:30,318 --> 00:03:31,950
since the twelve links do.

61
00:03:32,030 --> 00:03:36,203
On that reading, dependent arising
is simply the pattern of confusion,

62
00:03:36,283 --> 00:03:37,607
something to get out of.

63
00:03:38,408 --> 00:03:40,180
That reading needs refining.

64
00:03:40,260 --> 00:03:44,202
The twelve links, in forward order,
describe how suffering runs while

65
00:03:44,282 --> 00:03:45,656
ignorance is present.

66
00:03:45,736 --> 00:03:49,800
But dependent arising, as a view,
is not the shape of ignorance.

67
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:51,516
It is the antidote to it.

68
00:03:52,332 --> 00:03:54,879
Otherwise its praise would make no sense.

69
00:03:54,959 --> 00:03:57,786
Nāgārjuna bows to the
Buddha for teaching it,

70
00:03:57,866 --> 00:04:00,599
as the quieting of elaborations, peace.

71
00:04:00,679 --> 00:04:05,028
He says dependent arising, emptiness
and the middle way have one meaning.

72
00:04:05,108 --> 00:04:09,054
And it is said that whoever sees
dependent arising sees the Dhamma.

73
00:04:09,856 --> 00:04:12,253
So the same sentence does two things.

74
00:04:12,333 --> 00:04:15,487
Heard as production among
real things, when this is,

75
00:04:15,567 --> 00:04:17,756
that is, describes the trap.

76
00:04:17,836 --> 00:04:21,143
Seen as Nāgārjuna reads
it, it opens the way out.

77
00:04:21,956 --> 00:04:25,644
The tradition calls the ending
nirvāṇa, the ending of becoming.

78
00:04:25,724 --> 00:04:28,062
It is easy to picture this as a place.

79
00:04:28,142 --> 00:04:31,160
The round of birth and
death here, nirvāṇa there,

80
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:33,148
and a journey from one to the other.

81
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:36,710
Nāgārjuna does not let that picture stand.

82
00:04:36,790 --> 00:04:39,700
Nothing at all sets the
round apart from nirvāṇa.

83
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:43,454
And between their limits, not
even the finest gap is found.

84
00:04:44,260 --> 00:04:47,962
They are not two places, one
to leave and one to reach.

85
00:04:48,042 --> 00:04:51,902
To picture the ending of suffering as the
destruction of something real is itself

86
00:04:51,982 --> 00:04:53,206
the inherent view.

87
00:04:53,286 --> 00:04:57,382
Something can be cut off only if it
was there from its own side first.

88
00:04:58,184 --> 00:04:59,820
What ends was never a thing.

89
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:01,858
It was a way of taking things.

90
00:05:01,938 --> 00:05:03,665
Appearances do not end.

91
00:05:03,745 --> 00:05:05,758
The bell still rings when struck.

92
00:05:05,838 --> 00:05:07,809
The seed still gives rice.

93
00:05:07,889 --> 00:05:10,463
What ends is taking them
to stand on their own.

94
00:05:11,268 --> 00:05:14,521
One caution, and Nāgārjuna
gives it himself.

95
00:05:14,601 --> 00:05:17,633
Emptiness was taught as
the way out of all views.

96
00:05:17,713 --> 00:05:21,478
But those for whom emptiness
becomes a view, he calls incurable.

97
00:05:21,558 --> 00:05:25,667
Emptiness wrongly seen ruins, like
a snake grasped the wrong way.

98
00:05:26,464 --> 00:05:30,351
If emptiness becomes a new
thing, a void behind appearances,

99
00:05:30,431 --> 00:05:36,022
a state to reach, a view to defend, then
elaboration has simply found a new object.

100
00:05:36,836 --> 00:05:39,654
And seen rightly, emptiness
takes nothing away.

101
00:05:39,734 --> 00:05:43,595
For whom emptiness is possible,
everything is possible.

102
00:05:43,675 --> 00:05:47,358
It is because nothing has a nature
of its own that the links work,

103
00:05:47,438 --> 00:05:52,580
that karma holds, that practice changes
a person, and that the chain can end.

104
00:05:53,376 --> 00:05:56,113
Return once more to
the harsh word at work.

105
00:05:56,193 --> 00:05:59,550
In Section 5, the chain was
watched instead of obeyed.

106
00:05:59,630 --> 00:06:03,414
The first arrow landed, and
the second did not follow.

107
00:06:04,228 --> 00:06:07,726
Seen as Nāgārjuna reads it,
there is something further.

108
00:06:07,806 --> 00:06:13,256
The word, the hearing, the feeling and the
one who is hurt are found only together.

109
00:06:13,336 --> 00:06:17,033
The hurt is vivid, and it
follows its conditions exactly.

110
00:06:17,113 --> 00:06:20,171
But it was never a thing
that arrived from outside.

111
00:06:20,251 --> 00:06:22,717
And never a thing that
will be carried away.

112
00:06:23,528 --> 00:06:25,164
The afternoon goes on.

113
00:06:25,244 --> 00:06:29,689
The words were heard, the feeling
felt, a reply perhaps given.

114
00:06:29,769 --> 00:06:31,541
Nothing is taken from it.

115
00:06:32,340 --> 00:06:35,385
The tradition and Nāgārjuna
agree on the chain,

116
00:06:35,465 --> 00:06:39,520
on karma, on rebirth with no
traveller, and on the path.

117
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:41,952
Where they part is in what the pieces are.

118
00:06:42,032 --> 00:06:44,642
For the tradition, the person is empty.

119
00:06:44,722 --> 00:06:47,350
For Nāgārjuna, everything is.

120
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:52,265
This is Section 6, Part 3 of
the Dependent Arising series,

121
00:06:52,345 --> 00:06:54,389
and the close of Section 6.

122
00:06:55,196 --> 00:06:59,034
There was nothing to cut, because
nothing was ever tied on its own.

